From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] HID: magicmouse: let the MTP palm class be enabled on any SoC

The standard MTP finger record carries the controller's contact class in
the low byte of its second word (1 thumb, 2-3 finger, 6+ palm, recorded on
a T6041 J616C). The driver turns it into MT_TOOL_PALM only on T6041, so on
T6050 (J716s) libinput gets no palm flag at all: pressure is unusable
(INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD), edge palm zones are off for Apple touchpads, and
the contact-size threshold is the only palm signal left.

Add mtp_palm_class (read at probe, kernel command line
hid_magicmouse.mtp_palm_class=N): -1 keeps today's behaviour (T6041 only),
0 turns it off everywhere, 1 turns it on for every standard-layout MTP
trackpad so a SoC whose records have not been checked can be tried
without a rebuild. Once the J716s records are confirmed to use the same
classes (trackpad-feel/tp-contacts.py), a follow-up adds "apple,t6050" to
the -1 list.

With it on, the touch/approach ranges become 0..65534 (the T6041 setting)
and ABS_MT_TOOL_TYPE appears; libinput then marks such contacts as palms
(tp_palm_detect_tool_triggered) before any size check.

Base: j716s-series a0f2f30c967b (the running kernel). Not built.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
@@ -56,6 +56,16 @@
 static bool report_undeciphered;
 module_param(report_undeciphered, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(report_undeciphered, "Report undeciphered multi-touch state field using a MSC_RAW event");
+
+/*
+ * Whether the contact class in the standard MTP finger record is passed on
+ * as MT_TOOL_PALM. -1 picks the SoCs whose records were checked (T6041),
+ * 0 never does it, 1 does it on every standard-layout MTP trackpad, to try
+ * a SoC that has not been checked yet (hid_magicmouse.mtp_palm_class=1).
+ */
+static int mtp_palm_class = -1;
+module_param(mtp_palm_class, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(mtp_palm_class, "report the MTP controller's palm class as MT_TOOL_PALM: -1 checked SoCs only (T6041), 0 never, 1 every MTP trackpad (default -1)");
 
 /*
  * Waveform shaping, writable at runtime and applied on the next effect
@@ -2394,7 +2404,9 @@
 		np = of_get_child_by_name(dev_of_node(hdev->dev.parent), "multi-touch");
 		msc->mtp_c1fe = of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,j700-multitouch");
 		msc->mtp_palms = !msc->mtp_c1fe &&
-				 of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6041");
+				 (mtp_palm_class > 0 ||
+				  (mtp_palm_class < 0 &&
+				   of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6041")));
 		of_node_put(np);
 
 		msc->input_ops.raw_event = magicmouse_raw_event_mtp;
